module Core

# Each declaration below creates nothing: `@rf` names the shared declaration it shows, and validate-stdlib
# checks that the two still match.

### Represents the protocol for keyed, attack-resistant hashing.
### `Hashable` is the default hashing protocol used by `Set` and `Dict`. Its keyed
### form (SipHash-2-4 semantics) makes the probe sequence unpredictable to external
### attackers, so it is safe to use with untrusted input.
### `needs Hashable everywhere` auto-confers Hashable on any member-bearing type all of whose
### members are themselves Hashable — the structural gate that drives the auto-derived `hash`.
@rf("Hashable")
protocol Hashable
needs Hashable everywhere
    ### Returns a keyed hash of this value using SipHash-2-4 semantics.
    ### Implementations should incorporate the full logical value and produce the
    ### same result for equal values when called with the same key pair.
    ### :param k0: The first 64-bit key word.
    ### :param k1: The second 64-bit key word.
    ### :returns: The resulting `U64` value.
    routine Me.hash(k0: U64, k1: U64) -> U64
